        "original_id": "6dbed981-5588-5dcc-97ba-be5234f7d2ff",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Aeroflot, Moscow Airways, Babyflot airlines\n- Places: Russian Federation, Sheremetyevo International Airport, Canada\n- Concepts: breakup of the Soviet Union, dissolution of the Aeroflot monopoly\n- People: Zahra Kamalfar\n\nFacts:\n- In the early 1990s, the breakup of the Soviet Union and the dissolution of the Soviet airline monopoly Aeroflot led to the creation of former Soviet airlines informally called Babyflot.\n- Aeroflot is the flag carrier and largest airline of the Russian Federation.\n- Aeroflot is an open joint stock company that operates domestic and international passenger services mainly from its hub at Sheremetyevo International Airport.\n- Moscow Airways was a Russian airline formed as a subsidiary of Aeroflot to operate Aeroflot's fleet of Ilyushin Il-62 aircraft.\n- Zahra Kamalfar lived in Sheremetyevo International Airport for ten months and then went to Canada, where she had been residing since March 15, 2007.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
